# gitattributes-style rules for jj, applied by jj-diff-formatter.sh.
#
# jj ignores .gitattributes (https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/issues/53) and has no
# way to hide a file's diff (https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/issues/2915,
# https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/issues/4548), so this file is handed to
# `git diff` as core.attributesfile instead. `-diff` means "treat as binary":
# jj show / diff / log -p print "Binary files ... differ" for these.

*.pdf -diff
